<title>TURKEY: Turkey sells 257.8 trln lira 357-day bills.</title>
<headline>Turkey sells 257.8 trln lira 357-day bills.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Turkish Treasury met almost half of the bids in its 357-day bill auction on Tuesday by selling 257.8 trillion lira nominal-valued bills.</p>
<p>It had last sold 259.9 trillion lira of 357-day bills at 138.37 percent yield (including witholding tax) on August 12.</p>
<p>    Amount	: 257.8 trillion lira</p>
<p>    Total bids  : 545.0 trillion lira</p>
<p>    Max yield   : 138.38 percent (including witholding tax)</p>
<p>    Maturity    : August 12, 1998</p>
<p>    Value date  : August 20, 1997</p>
<p>The yield excluding witholding tax equals to 119.99 percent.</p>
<p>Banks will pay 107.4 trillion lira to the Treasury for the auction on Wednesday.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-275 08 75 EKS</p>
